proposed_comments.body:
### Reserve text-case hotkey IDs for existing settings

**Severity:** `high`

Existing Advanced Paste settings files do not contain the new `text-case` property. The Settings UI deserializes a default text-case group and includes its ten leaves when assigning IDs, while this runner path skips the group entirely when the JSON key is absent; custom-action IDs can therefore refer to different actions on the two sides. Insert a disabled in-memory default group when the persisted key is absent so the existing processing loop reserves the same ten IDs without enabling any shortcut.

```suggestion
                            L"text-case"
                        };

                        if (!additionalActions.HasKey(L"text-case"))
                        {
                            winrt::Windows::Data::Json::JsonObject textCaseActions;
                            static constexpr std::array textCaseActionIds{
                                L"lower-case",
                                L"upper-case",
                                L"title-case",
                                L"sentence-case",
                                L"toggle-case",
                                L"camel-case",
                                L"pascal-case",
                                L"snake-case",
                                L"screaming-snake-case",
                                L"kebab-case",
                            };

                            for (const auto actionId : textCaseActionIds)
                            {
                                winrt::Windows::Data::Json::JsonObject action;
                                action.Insert(JSON_KEY_IS_SHOWN, winrt::Windows::Data::Json::JsonValue::CreateBooleanValue(false));
                                action.Insert(JSON_KEY_SHORTCUT, winrt::Windows::Data::Json::JsonObject{});
                                textCaseActions.Insert(actionId, action);
                            }

                            additionalActions.Insert(L"text-case", textCaseActions);
                        }
```

